                <!-- Job 1 -->
                <div class="xp-detail-pane">
                  <div class="xp-job-header">
                    <div>
                      <div class="xp-job-title">Senior Software Engineer</div>
                      <div class="xp-job-company">EmTech Care Labs | Portland, ME</div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="xp-job-date">Jan 2025 - Present</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="xp-job-description">
                    Sole senior engineer on a HIPAA-compliant platform that helps families coordinate Alzheimer's
                    care. 200+ caregivers and patients use it for real-time messaging, push notifications, and shared
                    care plans, all running on AWS. I made it audit-ready for healthcare data with encrypted patient
                    information, full audit logging, and role-based access, and it cleared an outside HIPAA readiness
                    review with no critical findings. I also merged three separate web and mobile codebases into one
                    TypeScript monorepo, scoped features directly with clinicians, and mentored two junior engineers.
                  </div>
                </div>
                <hr class="xp-job-separator">

                <!-- Job 2 -->
                <div class="xp-detail-pane">
                  <div class="xp-job-header">
                    <div>
                      <div class="xp-job-title">Senior Software Engineer</div>
                      <div class="xp-job-company">AllFactors | Santa Clara, CA</div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="xp-job-date">Oct 2021 - Dec 2024</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="xp-job-description">
                    Rebuilt a slow legacy real-estate analytics app on Blazor WebAssembly. Page loads got about twice
                    as fast, and the brittle state management that had made the old app risky to touch went away with
                    it. I also built a real-time market-data pipeline on SignalR and SQL Server change tracking that
                    streamed live pricing and inventory to hundreds of concurrent users in under a second, plus a
                    reusable library of data grids, charts, and filters that every dashboard in the product ended up
                    built on.
                  </div>
                </div>
                <hr class="xp-job-separator">

                <!-- Job 3 -->
                <div class="xp-detail-pane">
                  <div class="xp-job-header">
                    <div>
                      <div class="xp-job-title">Software Engineer</div>
                      <div class="xp-job-company">Smart Meal Service | Russia</div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="xp-job-date">Sep 2020 - Jul 2021</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="xp-job-description">
                    Wrote the C# / .NET software running a self-service food kiosk and a robotic cashier, down to the
                    low-level protocols for the payment terminals and the hardware. Also built the customer ordering
                    app (Xamarin) and the admin dashboard (ASP.NET Core and Angular). Automated order routing cut
                    kitchen wait times noticeably, and a hardware abstraction layer let one codebase run on all three
                    machine models.
                  </div>
                </div>
                <hr class="xp-job-separator">

                <!-- Job 4 -->
                <div class="xp-detail-pane">
                  <div class="xp-job-header">
                    <div>
                      <div class="xp-job-title">Game Developer</div>
                      <div class="xp-job-company">Pentalight Technology | Malaysia</div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="xp-job-date">Mar 2020 - Feb 2021</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="xp-job-description">
                    Built the multiplayer networking for a VR smart-city simulation in Unity, so everyone in a session
                    saw the same world in real time. Also did the spatial audio, the hand tracking, and the in-world
                    interfaces, plus a desktop spectator client for people without a headset. Automating the art
                    pipeline turned a multi-hour job per scene into something an artist could start and walk away
                    from.
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
