                <!-- Research 2 -->
                <li class="xp-research-item">
                  <div class="xp-research-icon"><i class="fas fa-image"></i></div>
                  <div class="xp-research-content">
                    <div class="xp-research-title">Localize, Don't Beautify: Controlling Image-Editing APIs</div>
                    <div class="xp-research-desc">
                      Ask a commercial image editor to change one feature of a face and it beautifies the whole thing,
                      which is a problem when the picture is meant to be a surgical preview. I tested how much of that
                      can be fixed from the client side, without touching the model. Across six editors, plain masked
                      compositing localized better than model-based inpainting.
                    </div>
                    <div class="xp-research-tags">
                      <span>Image-Editing APIs</span>
                      <span>Inpainting</span>
                      <span>ArcFace</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="xp-research-links">
                      <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.02841" target="_blank">
                        <i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i> arXiv Paper
                      </a>
                    </div>
