                      <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.09289" target="_blank">
                        <i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i> arXiv Paper
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </li>
                <!-- Research 4 -->
                <li class="xp-research-item">
                  <div class="xp-research-icon"><i class="fas fa-eye"></i></div>
                  <div class="xp-research-content">
                    <div class="xp-research-title">LightDepth: Lightweight Monocular Depth Estimation (course project)</div>
                    <div class="xp-research-desc">
                      A ResNet18 encoder with a U-Net decoder for monocular depth. It holds accuracy at 14.3M
                      parameters where Depth Anything V2 needs 24.8M, runs 72% faster at inference, and comes out
                      slightly ahead on relative error on NYU Depth V2.
                    </div>
                    <div class="xp-research-tags">
                      <span>PyTorch</span>
                      <span>ResNet18</span>
                      <span>U-Net</span>
                      <span>Depth Estimation</span>
                    </div>
